# Go service

Quality thresholds: **`quality-and-testing.mdc`**. API/HTTP semantics: **`api-and-events.mdc`**. Security: **`security-baseline.mdc`**. Pins: `.agents-v0/packs/go/PACK.md`.

## Source layout

A new service uses Gin. Packages under the module: `api`, `service`, `repository`, `domain`. golang-migrate SQL lives in `db/migrations`. An existing chi or `net/http` router stays. Do not add Gin beside it, or `pom.xml`.

## Shape

- Handlers take a service constructed in `main`. No package-level database handle.
- Handlers decode a request struct and call the service. Do not return repository rows.
- SQL uses placeholders. Sort and filter fields come from an allowlist.
- `log/slog` with structured fields. Do not log tokens, secrets, or raw PII.
- No empty error discard. Functions ≤ 30 lines.
- Correlation id and `traceparent` on every request.
